{"id": 82, "ts": 1784191233.3639765, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I agree with Agent\u202f1 that Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall fit. While we still lack concrete data on his crew\u2011cooperation and stress\u2011resilience, the facts we do have are compelling for a long\u2011distance pilot: he can anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, has excellent spatial vision, and demonstrates very good leadership qualities. Those attributes directly support the criteria of operational reliability (anticipating hazards), technical competence, and decision quality on complex, high\u2011risk routes. The concerns \u2013 being perceived as a show\u2011off and not open to new ideas \u2013 are outweighed by the lack of comparable safety\u2011critical strengths in the other candidates. Candidate\u202fB, despite being conscientious and stress\u2011resilient, makes nasty remarks about colleagues and has a weak numerical memory, raising serious crew\u2011cooperation and attention\u2011to\u2011detail issues. Candidate\u202fA is perfectly reliable and calm but struggles to communicate ideas and is egocentric, which could impair cockpit coordination. Candidate\u202fD shows responsibility and problem\u2011solving but is described as a know\u2011it\u2011all with a hot temper, and we have no evidence of effective crew interaction. Given the current evidence, I maintain my provisional vote for Candidate\u202fC."}
